  "problem": "$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.3\\end{aligned}],\\,q=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the stochastic matrix $P$ and vector $q$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $q$ is a stochastic vector\n- $Pq=q$\n- $q$ is a steady-state vector of $P$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that a steady-state vector of a stochastic matrix $P$ is a stochastic vector $q$ such that $Pq=q.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector since its entries are non-negative and add up to $1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, we have \n\n$$\nPq=[\\begin{aligned}0.2 & 0.7 \\\\ 0.8 & 0.3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1.4}{15}+\\frac{5.6}{15} \\\\ \\frac{5.6}{15}+\\frac{2.4}{15}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{15} \\\\ \\frac{8}{15}\\end{aligned}]=q.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, $q$ is a stochastic vector such that $Pq=q.$ So, it's a steady-state vector of $P.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
